    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it sounds crazy but the pattern is too consistent for just an HVAC system. like, it changes slightly depending on the barometric pressure. if someone wanted to use atmospheric ducts or something like ionospheric reflection to bounce a signal, could they use those pressure spikes to maintain a stable transmission? i just feel like i'm picking up on something intentional.",
